# Build-context filter for docker/Dockerfile.apiserver.
#
# WHY THIS FILE HAS THIS NAME, AND WHY IT IS NOT ../.dockerignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker normally reads the .dockerignore at the root of the build CONTEXT. This image's context
# is the PARENT of this repo (it needs both graphql-api/ and ncog-evm/, because go.mod carries
#     replace github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum => ../ncog-evm
# ) -- and that same parent is ALSO the context for the node image in the sibling ncogearthchain
# repo. There is only one <context>/.dockerignore, the node repo's `make ncogearthchain-image`
# overwrites it from its own canonical copy, and that copy denies `*` and re-admits only
# `ncogearthchain` and `ncog-evm`. Under it, graphql-api/ is not in the context at all and this
# build dies on its first COPY.
#
# BuildKit resolves `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` in preference to the context-root file. So
# naming this file after the Dockerfile gives the two images independent, non-conflicting filters
# over a shared context, with neither repo reaching into the other or into the parent directory.
# It is also why this Dockerfile requires BuildKit (Docker 23+ / buildx): a legacy builder ignores
# this file and falls back to the context-root one.
#
# Docker applies the LAST matching pattern, so the order of the three sections below is
# load-bearing.
#
# CAUTION when editing section 3: broad `**/<name>` patterns are dangerous here because both
# admitted trees are Go source whose package directories have ordinary names -- `**/build` would
# silently delete ncog-evm/build (which holds ci.go, referenced by its Makefile) and `**/keystore`
# would delete ncog-evm/accounts/keystore. Prefer repo-rooted paths, as below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Deny every top-level entry.
#    `*` matches a single path segment, so this excludes ncogearthchain/, wallet/,
#    ncog-explorer/, nec-node-sdk/, ncog-trimix-ide/, genesis/, docs/, transactions.rlp --
#    everything. Unfiltered this parent directory is ~7.4 GB; none of it is reachable from
#    `go build ./cmd/apiserver`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Re-admit exactly the two trees this build needs.
#    ncogearthchain/ is deliberately NOT here: the explorer talks to the node over RPC and does
#    not import it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!graphql-api
!ncog-evm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Strip what those two trees do not need in order to compile.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version metadata comes in as --build-arg and the build runs with -buildvcs=false, so no .git is
# needed. Together they are ~18 MB and they change on every commit, which would also bust the
# COPY cache layer on every build for nothing.
graphql-api/.git
ncog-evm/.git

# BUILD ARTEFACTS. The two Windows binaries in this repo's root are why this section exists:
# apiserver.exe (35 MB) and migrate.exe (15 MB) sit beside go.mod, are ignored by .gitignore
# (`*.exe`) and so are untracked, and would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon and baked into
# the builder layer on every build -- 50 MB of a foreign OS's binaries inside a Linux image.
# `make server` output lands in build/ for the same reason.
graphql-api/*.exe
graphql-api/*.test
graphql-api/build
graphql-api/vendor
ncog-evm/build/_workspace
ncog-evm/build/_bin
ncog-evm/build/bin
ncog-evm/vendor

# LOCAL CREDENTIALS. internal/config/load.go adds "." to viper's search path and keys.go names
# the file "apiserver", so a config in this repo's ROOT is loaded automatically -- and
# doc/postgres-cutover.md documents exactly that file carrying a live Postgres DSN with a
# password. It is gitignored, so it is invisible to git-based hygiene but very much present in a
# `docker build` context. It must never reach a layer.
graphql-api/apiserver.json
graphql-api/apiserver.yaml
graphql-api/apiserver.yml
graphql-api/apiserver.toml
graphql-api/.env
graphql-api/.env.*

# ncog-evm/tests/testdata is a git submodule of the Ethereum consensus test vectors, and
# ncog-evm/docs is prose. Neither is compiled, and neither tree has a go:embed reaching outside
# its own package.
ncog-evm/tests/testdata
ncog-evm/docs

# Editor and CI config: not compiled.
graphql-api/.github
graphql-api/.idea
graphql-api/.vscode
ncog-evm/.github
ncog-evm/.idea
ncog-evm/.vscode

# Recursive globs, kept deliberately few and checked against
# `find graphql-api ncog-evm -type d -name <n>` (all returned nothing) before being added.
**/node_modules
**/*.ipc
**/*.log
**/*.prof
**/.DS_Store
